REGIONAL REGULATION OF EAST KUTAI REGENCY

NUMBER 3 OF 2023

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN

BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

THE REGENT OF EAST KUTAI,

Considering:

a. that every woman has the right to protection of her person, family, honor, dignity, and property under her control, and has the right to a sense of security and protection from threats of fear to do or not do something which is a basic right;
b. that to provide a guideline or reference for local government and related stakeholders regarding the improvement of women's quality of life and protection of women, especially for women victims of violence;
c. that to provide direction, foundation and legal certainty to all parties involved in the empowerment of women and children, it is necessary to regulate the establishment of an Integrated Service Center for the Protection of Women and Children;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a through c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Women;

In View of:
1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 47 of 1999 concerning the Establishment of Nunukan Regency, Malinau Regency, West Kutai Regency, East Kutai Regency and Bontang City (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 175, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3896) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 3 of 2022 concerning the State Capital (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2022 Number 41, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6766);
3. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587), as amended several times, most recently by Law Number 6 of 2023 concerning the Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 2 of 2022 concerning Job Creation into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2023 Number 41, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6856);
4. Regulation of the Minister of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 6 of 2015 concerning the System for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;
5. Regulation of the Minister of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 4 of 2018 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment of Regional Technical Implementation Units for the Protection of Women and Children.

With Mutual Approval of

THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF EAST KUTAI REGENCY

and

THE REGENT OF EAST KUTAI

DECIDES:

To Establish:

REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING THE PROTECTION OF WOMEN.

Article 2

This Regional Regulation is implemented based on the principles of:
a. respect for human rights;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. non-discrimination; and
d. the best interests of women.

Article 3

This Regional Regulation aims to:
a. guarantee the fulfillment of women's rights so that they can live and participate optimally in accordance with human dignity and dignity;
b. prevent all forms of Violence against Women;
c. provide protection and a sense of security for women victims of violence and discrimination;
d. guarantee the implementation of policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women by the region in a systematic, comprehensive, sustainable, and integrated manner;
e. increase the commitment of the Regional Government in implementing policies, programs and activities for the protection of women; and
f. encourage institutions that handle the duties and functions of women's empowerment in the Regional Government and community institutions in the region to improve performance in efforts to protect women.

Article 4

The scope of this Regional Regulation includes:
a. the rights of women victims of violence;
b. the authority of the Regional Government;
c. planning;
d. implementation;
e. monitoring and evaluation;
f. reporting;
g. guidance and supervision;
h. community participation; and
i. funding.

CHAPTER II

RIGHTS OF WOMEN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

Article 5

Every woman victim of violence has the right:
a. to have her dignity and worth as a human being respected;
b. to obtain protection from family, community, Regional Government and/or other parties either temporarily or based on a protection order from the court;
c. to physical, psychological and sexual health recovery in accordance with the suffering experienced by Women Victims of Violence;
d. to special handling related to the confidentiality of Women Victims of Violence;
e. to assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
f. to spiritual guidance services; and
g. to make her own decisions.

Article 10

Prevention of acts of violence against women as referred to in article 6 paragraph (2) letter a, the Regional Government shall undertake the following efforts:
a. conduct counseling and socialization regarding matters relating to violence against women;
b. conduct socialization on women's rights;
c. seek to improve education for women;
d. open skills courses for women to support the economic needs of families;
e. create employment opportunities for women;
f. provide counseling to immediately report to local authorities if violence against women occurs;
g. empower social community organizations and women's organizations to increase women's knowledge and insight;
h. establish Women Protection Complaint Posts; and
i. form networks in efforts to prevent violence.

Article 11

1. The provision of Services for Women victims of violence includes, among others:
a. providing Services and handling as quickly as possible to Women Victims of Violence;
b. providing convenience, comfort, safety, and free of charge for Women Victims of Violence;
c. maintaining the confidentiality of Women Victims of Violence; and
d. guaranteeing justice and legal certainty for Women Victims of Violence.

Article 15

1. The procedures and mechanisms of integrated Services include:
a. complaint services;
b. Health Rehabilitation;
c. Social Rehabilitation;
d. Repatriation;
e. Social Reintegration, and
f. Legal Aid.
2. The implementation of integrated services as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out in accordance with SPM.

Part Five

Article 16

1. SPM in the field of integrated services for women and children victims of violence aims to ensure that Women Victims of violence receive the minimum services needed.
2. SPM in the field of integrated services for Women Victims of violence includes services for:
a. handling complaints/reports of Victims of Violence Against Women;
b. health services for women Victims of violence;
c. social rehabilitation for women Victims of violence;
d. law enforcement and Legal Aid for women Victims of violence;
e. Repatriation and Social Reintegration for women Victims of violence; and
f. in the event that Women Victims of Violence experience trauma or illness that endangers themselves as a result of acts of violence requiring immediate assistance, the Regional Government is obliged to provide first aid no later than 7 (seven) days after the complaint is filed.

Article 17

SPM as referred to in Article 16 has women performance including:
a. coverage of women victims of violence who receive complaint handling by trained officers within the integrated Service unit;
b. coverage of Women Victims of violence who receive indicator services by trained indicator personnel at health centers and hospitals;
c. coverage of Social Rehabilitation services provided by trained Social Rehabilitation officers for indicator Victims of violence within the integrated Service unit;
d. coverage of indicator guidance services provided by trained indicator guidance officers for Women Victims of Violence within the integrated Service unit;
e. coverage of law enforcement from the investigation level to court decisions on cases of Violence Against Women;
f. coverage of Women Victims of Violence who receive Legal Aid services;
g. coverage of Repatriation services for Women Victims of Violence; and
h. coverage of Social Reintegration services for Women Victims of Violence.
2. The determination of SPM performance indicators in the field of integrated services for Women Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) constitutes a minimum target that must be achieved by the integrated service unit in stages.

CHAPTER IX

COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION

Article 25

1. In organizing the Protection of Women, the community may:
a. establish family partners at the sub-district/village level;
b. establish women's protection units within community organizations;
c. conduct independent socialization of Women's rights;
d. provide first aid to Women Victims of Violence;
e. report to the competent authorities if violence against Women occurs in their environment.
f. prevent acts of violence against women.
g. provide information and/or report acts of violence against women to the competent authorities; and
h. forms and roles of the community are carried out responsibly in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
2. Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:
a. Individuals;
b. social community institutions;
c. non-governmental organizations;
d. educational institutions;
e. religious institutions;
f. private sector; and
g. mass media.
